G1: Production Build Runs Against Embedded SQLite — VERIFIED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✅ Real `next build` + real `node server.js` (not `next dev`), real HTTP 200s, real login
     against embedded SQLite.
  ✅ Real bug found and fixed: relative SQLite DATABASE_URL resolves against the generated
     Prisma client's own directory, not CWD - absolute path required.
  ✅ Journal Entry 1, DECISIONS.md D-049.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G2: Bundled Self-Contained Node Runtime — VERIFIED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✅ Official Node 20.20.2 LTS, checksum-verified, downloaded with the owner's explicit
     permission. Self-containment proven at the OS level (Get-Process on the real serving PID
     showed the bundled node.exe path, not system Node).
  ✅ Two real bugs found and fixed: the Prisma CLI shim isn't JS (calls the real entry point
     now); /api/health/status and /api/health/detailed were silently statically frozen at
     build time (force-dynamic added, re-verified live).
  ✅ Journal Entry 2, DECISIONS.md D-050.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G3: First-Run Lifecycle Against a Fresh Packaged Database — VERIFIED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✅ Built the missing first-run admin setup (POST /api/setup, one-time-only) and admin-only
     user creation (POST /api/users) - no hard-coded credentials anywhere, closing a real gap
     (previously only a broken dev fixture or a hard-coded-password demo seed script existed).
  ✅ Full real lifecycle executed via HTTP against the packaged app: admin setup -> QM
     ingests evidence -> event -> causal-status chain -> intervention -> atom authored and
     approved -> frozen manifest compiled and assigned -> learner completes -> supervisor
     observes -> real automatic closure. Independently reconfirmed via a direct DB query,
     bypassing the API entirely.
  ✅ Journal Entry 3, DECISIONS.md D-051.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G4: Stop/Restart Persistence, Backup + Restore — VERIFIED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✅ Restart: real PID confirmed dead (not assumed), relaunched as a genuinely new PID,
     byte-for-byte diff of every record including the frozen manifest's hash: identical.
  ✅ Backup/restore into a completely separate clean directory tree (not over the live
     install): real SHA-256, real login proving the password hash survived, byte-for-byte
     diff: identical.
  ✅ Real gap found and fixed: start.ps1 previously treated "no DB file" as always meaning
     fresh install - the classic silent-data-loss trap. Added a data/.initialized marker +
     db-check.mjs preflight integrity/table-count check. Three real negative scenarios
     (missing/corrupted/zero-byte DB, marker present) each confirmed to fail loudly, exit
     non-zero, never bind the port.
  ✅ Separate real gap found via due-diligence re-testing outside the repo: the packaged app/
     silently depended on the repo's own node_modules for the Prisma CLI's dependencies,
     invisible while testing from inside the checkout. Fixed, re-verified in genuine
     isolation.
  ✅ Journal Entry 4, DECISIONS.md D-052.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G5: INSTALL-GUIDE.md, Self-Validated in Genuine Isolation — VERIFIED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✅ docs/03-architecture/INSTALL-GUIDE.md written as a validation protocol (every step ends
     with an observable "You should now see" check).
  ✅ Real distributable built (HF-Engine-Standalone-Windows.zip) and the guide walked
     literally, step by step, in an environment with zero repo tree above it.
  ✅ Most significant finding of the whole directive, found via this self-validation: the
     session cookie was marked Secure with no HTTPS anywhere in the product's design - every
     real-browser login silently failed to stay logged in, never caught by G1-G4's curl-based
     testing (curl doesn't enforce that browser policy). Fixed (isSecureDeployment(), keyed
     off NEXTAUTH_URL's real scheme) and re-verified live in a real browser. Logged as an
     appended correction to G1-G4's login evidence, not a rewrite - their specific claims
     remain true; only "stays logged in for a real browser" was unproven until this gate.
  ✅ Full disaster-recovery walk: real login as a QM account, original password, correct
     role-routed page, after a genuine backup -> restore -> fresh-location round trip.
  ✅ Journal Entry 5, DECISIONS.md D-053.

